#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Ohio  -  PyQt6   (rofi-style launcher)
-------------------------------------
Header buttons (left -> right):
    moon / sun  = switch DARK <-> LIGHT mode
    terminal    = FILES mode: every public file + folder in your user profile,
                  sortable by Name / Modified / Size / Type  (System32, AppData,
                  Program Files, hidden + system stuff is never shown)
    window      = APPS mode (default)
    gear        = SETTINGS: paste a banner / background path, blur, tilt, accent ...

Keys:
    type        filter            Up/Down  move          Enter  launch / open
    Shift+Enter reveal file in its folder                Tab    apps <-> files
    Ctrl+,      settings                                 Esc    close
    ">cmd"      run a command     "?words"  web search

NEW in this version
    * going into / out of a folder slides the old list away and the new rows fly in
    * the path bar slides open, the path is "typed" out with a caret, the ">" button ripples
    * header buttons squish when held, bounce + ripple on click, and their icons spin / wiggle
    * the sort bar slides open, the accent pill glides between chips, the arrow rotates,
      chips pop in one by one, hover fades, click bounce, status text slides

FIXES in this build (nothing else was changed)
    * scrolling fast:  rows are snapped to whole pixels + hard-clipped to the list, icons are
      never loaded inside paintEvent any more, the intro stagger now really finishes
    * missing apps:    Start-menu .url / .appref-ms shortcuts (Steam games ...) and every
      Store / UWP app (Calculator, Photos, Settings ...) are listed now
    * lag / freezes:   only the part of the window that changed is repainted, the file indexer
      no longer fights the UI thread for the GIL, sorting 100k+ files is lazy, fonts are cached

Settings are saved to  ~/.config/quick_launcher/config.json

Install:  pip install PyQt6
Run:      python ohio.py
          python ohio.py --bg "C:/Pictures/bg.jpg" --banner "C:/Pictures/banner.png"
"""
